<h4>Strategies</h4>
<table class="two-column-text">
<thead>
<tr>
<th class="ou-help mceNonEditable" width="50%">Column 1</th>
<th class="ou-help mceNonEditable" width="50%">Column 2</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>
<ul>
<li>Recruit world-class faculty: Execute strategic high-quality faculty recruitments in AI, cybersecurity and computing to build critical mass for large-scale grants via cluster hires, targeted hiring and regular hiring.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Center-level grants: Pursue large-scale (&gt; $5 million) funding with Bellini College faculty as principal investigators by leveraging the new college structure to unify dispersed research efforts and address convergent problems responsibly and ethically; provide college-level travel funds for envisioning workshops for these grants.&nbsp;</li>
<li>REU sites: Increase the number of National Science Foundation REU Site grants; leverage resources at CRA to structure undergraduate research programming; leverage external funds, such as from CRA, FHTC.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Network building: Build partnerships with funded AI/cybersecurity institutes across the nation; engage top faculty members from other universities in proposal studios and external red‑team reviews.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
</td>
<td>
<ul>
<li>Ph.D. recruitment: Build recruitment strategies for domestic students; offer multiple-year offers for high-quality students; leverage university-level scholarships.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Centers and institutes: Formulate governance and faculty-hiring policies for centers and institutes in the college; nurture the AI+X Institute and CITA; establish a center/institute for cybersecurity research and education; launch a fourth center or institute on an appropriate topic; encourage annual symposia.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Nominate faculty for external awards: Utilize USF Awards and Honors resources to nominate faculty for external awards and honors; invite speakers who are National Academy members for campus visits.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h4><span style="color: #3f565e; font-size: 1.125em;">Success Indicators&nbsp;</span></h4>
<ul>
<li>Total annual research expenditures: Track growth from the current $4 million baseline to $10 million, comparable to the top 25 public computing units.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Faculty awards: Number of faculty members inducted into National Academies (preeminence metric) or receiving highly prestigious awards (e.g., NSF CAREER, Fellows of ACM, AAAS, or IEEE).&nbsp;</li>
<li>Undergraduate research: Secure faculty commitment for 100 Research Experiences for Undergraduates (REU) per year.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Ph.D. students: Build a resilient and sustainable doctoral program by achieving a target enrollment of five Ph.D. students per tenure-track faculty member.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Faculty headcount growth: Track recruitment toward the target of 100 total faculty (75 tenure-track and 25 instructional) within five years to stabilize student-to-faculty ratios.&nbsp;</li>
<li>National ranking: Achieve and maintain a Faculty Scholarly Productivity Index that places the Bellini College within the top 25 of U.S. public computing units as benchmarked by Academic Analytics.</li>
</ul><!-- /com.omniupdate.div -->
</maincontent>

